WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:06.525
Tonight’s lights belong to the two kinds of vessel that stand above you on the ladder: sail and fishing.

2
00:00:06.775 --> 00:00:10.875
If you can’t recognize them in the dark, you can’t give way to them.

3
00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:14.550
We’ll start with Rule twenty-five, sailing vessels.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.875
A sailing vessel underway shows sidelights and a sternlight.

5
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:20.750
And that’s all.

6
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.675
What’s missing?

7
00:00:23.675 --> 00:00:25.475
The masthead light.

8
00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:27.625
No white light forward.

9
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:33.175
So red and green with no white above them is a boat under sail, coming at you.

10
00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:41.200
On a sailing vessel under twenty meters, those three lights can be combined in one lantern at or near the top of the mast.

11
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:43.650
Sailors call it a tricolor.

12
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.725
It’s high up, so it shows over the waves.

13
00:00:46.975 --> 00:00:53.075
And a sailing vessel may add two all-round lights at or near the masthead: red over green.

14
00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:55.850
Red over green, sailing machine.

15
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.425
She shows those along with her sidelights and sternlight.

16
00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:03.375
But she can’t show them together with the tricolor lantern.
